  "question": {
    "text": "A battery of internal resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> is connected to the network of resistances as shown in the figure. In order that the maximum power be delivered to the network, the value of <em><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math></em>&nbsp;(in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>) should be<br />\r<br />\r<style type=\"text/css\"><!--\r\t\t@page { margin: 2cm }\r\t\tP { margin-bottom: 0.21cm }\r\t-->\r</style>\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0103_ea73a0d6a953.jpg\" style=\"width: 390px; height: 164px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "The given circuit is a balanced Wheatstone's bridge.<br /><br /><style type=\"text/css\"><!--\t\t@page { margin: 2cm }\t\tP { margin-bottom: 0.21cm }\t--></style><strong><u><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0103_bed379d582d8.jpg\" style=\"width: 456px; height: 200px;\" /></u></strong><br /><br />Thus, no current will flow across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi>R</mi></math>. The given circuit will now be equivalent to:-<br /><br /><style type=\"text/css\"><!--\t\t@page { margin: 2cm }\t\tP { margin-bottom: 0.21cm }\t--></style><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0103_f29bf801a742.jpg\" /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0103_677ed3ea30db.jpg\" style=\"width: 348px; height: 177px;\" /><br /><br />For maximum power, net external resistance = Total internal resistance<br />or&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math><br />or&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>"
  }
}